Firewall Map+ shows the firewall's live traffic on a world map, as a
dashboard widget and a full-size page. Connections come from PF state
counters and are geolocated locally (MaxMind GeoLite2 or DB-IP Lite); blocked
attempts come from the filter log and Suricata alerts from its EVE log. Each
connection is described in plain language (who opened it, service, the other
side's network and country, allowed or blocked). Traffic involving addresses
in threat lists, the AbuseIPDB blacklist or Suricata alerts is flagged and
recorded in Threats by observed disposition, with on-demand registry, routing
and AbuseIPDB lookups. IPv4 and IPv6 are supported throughout. No firewall
rules are changed.
